<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7406" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρροιβδ-έω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναροιβδέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>swallow back, suck down again,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάρυβδις ἀναρροιβδεῖ μέλαν ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.104
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς δ᾽ ἀναροιβδεῖ</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				105
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				236
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Sect.Intr.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; but in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				440
			</span></i>, <i>throw up,</i> as expl. by Phot.<i><span class="en">
				p.120
			</span></i> R., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.10
			</span></i>. (The spelling <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρρυβδ-</span>
			has Ms. authority in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and is supported by the assonance with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάρυβδις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταρυβδήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			)</div>
